I've applied 7 update rules to create a clean, borderless display of pure images on the Pinterest search grid:

1. **Hide text overlays below pins** (`.To17G1.ekBBbl`) — This hides the entire metadata section beneath each pin that contains descriptions, board names, creator info, and the overflow menu button.

2. **Remove pin card borders/padding** (`[data-test-id="pin"]`) — Removes any borders or padding on the pin card container.

3. **Remove masonry container padding** (`.masonryContainer`) — Removes the 8px horizontal padding from the masonry grid container.

4. **Hide content layer overlays** (`[data-test-id="contentLayer"]`) — Hides any overlay content that might appear on top of pin images.

5. **Hide image overlay elements** (`.SXrTgC`) — Hides potential watermark/creator tag overlays within the image wrapper.

6. **Remove grid item borders** (`[data-grid-item="true"]`) — Ensures no borders on the grid positioning containers.

7. **Remove pin wrapper borders** (`[data-test-id="pinWrapper"]`) — Removes any borders or padding from the direct image wrapper.

This should give you a clean, borderless masonry grid of pure Pinterest images with all text overlays, attributions, and creator tags hidden.

